  "overview": "**Vuetify** is a light-first design system anchored on `#FFFFFF` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#FF8A80` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `System UI` (57px display down to 16px body), unified by `4px` base corner radius and subtle shadow elevation.\n\nSource: published token package (https://vuetifyjs.com), package `vuetify`. Inventory: **90** colors, **117** typography steps, and **31** documented components (MIT license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 31 component tokens with documented paddings: `0`, `8px 12px`, `2px`, `6px 12px`, `10px 14px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#EEEEEE` cards; separate sibling sections using `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Layered Shadow Model**: Uses documented shadows (`0 0 0 0 rgba(,.3),0 0 0 0 rgba(,.15)`) paired with `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` borders for elevated overlays.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#FF8A80` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#FFFFFF` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#FF8A80` with `#0b0b0c` text (8.6:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `System UI` headings with `System UI` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `4px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (4px on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `#EEEEEE` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `4px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `v-otp-input` fields and secondary buttons."
}
